      {
        "id": 18550,
        "name": "Disgruntled",
        "username": "Disgruntled",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/958977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-17T23:34:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My wife and I play a ton of SotM. We have been anxiously waiting for the release of Oblivaeon since the late cretacious period. The choice was made not to be a backer on Kickstarter because we have had bad dealings with them in the past and generally to not like encouraging preorder as a business model. So we regularly checked online stores hoping to see a 'buy' button instead of a 'pre-order' button. We saw that at&nbsp;https://store.greaterthangames.com/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-oblivaeon.html there was no information indicating the product was out of stock or back ordered and decided to buy.</p>\n<p>We immediately noticed, in the confirmation email that the status was 'back-ordered.' Following the website's instruction we contacted contact@greaterthangames.com and politely asked for clarity. There was no reply. We sent the email again after several weeks. There was no reply. We saw some information posted to a third party website, kickstarter.com, but as we made no purchase through that website, we waited and sent another email.</p>\n<p>I had no interest in preordering a product. I would not have ordered if there was any indication that it would have taken months (it is yet to arrive). I have used the contact method requested by the company, to no avail.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>EDIT:</p>\n<p>After posting here greater than games contacted me and addressed all of my concerns.</p>\n<p>Thanks guys!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span>Caleb</span></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:56.759Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
