        "raw": "<p>My wife and I play a ton of SotM. We have been anxiously waiting for the release of Oblivaeon since the late cretacious period. The choice was made not to be a backer on Kickstarter because we have had bad dealings with them in the past and generally to not like encouraging preorder as a business model. So we regularly checked online stores hoping to see a 'buy' button instead of a 'pre-order' button. We saw that at&nbsp;https://store.greaterthangames.com/sentinels-of-the-multiverse-oblivaeon.html there was no information indicating the product was out of stock or back ordered and decided to buy.</p>\r\n<p>We immediately noticed, in the confirmation email that the status was 'back-ordered.' Following the website's instruction we contacted contact@greaterthangames.com and politely asked for clarity. There was no reply. We sent the email again after several weeks. There was no reply. We saw some information posted to a third party website, kickstarter.com, but as we made no purchase through that website, we waited and sent another email.</p>\r\n<p>I had no interest in preordering a product. I would not have ordered if there was any indication that it would have taken months (it is yet to arrive). I have used the contact method requested by the company, to no avail.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>EDIT:</p>\r\n<p>After posting here greater than games contacted me and addressed all of my concerns.</p>\r\n<p>Thanks guys!</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span>Caleb</span></p>",
